{"title":"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Based_on_Official_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Based on Official Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An airplane holds a maximum of 245 passengers. To accommodate the extra expense of transporting luggage, passengers are charged a baggage fee of \\$20 for the first bag checked plus \\$7 for each additional bag checked. (Passengers who do not check a bag are not charged a baggage fee.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On one flight, 200 passengers checked exactly one bag and the other 45 passengers checked exactly two bags. Determine the total of the baggage fees for checked bags.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Based_on_Official_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Based_on_Official_Solution_2)\">Solution 1 (Based on Official Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Based on Official Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the plane was completely full, there must have been <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/4129eebb0569e831f5875a3c47a0b96cf6903768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$245$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> passengers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of passengers that checked one bag. This makes the number of passengers that checked two bags <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a606048188330b78bf95cbe08c39351e7cee07a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$245 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using similar logic as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 2a\">part a</a>, the passengers that checked one bag would have paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555360df10d7f3448442d43c277f763b0d1236bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> each, while the passengers that checked two bags would have paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30a9e03ced4d2b7794f7535308a84a17d0a06c39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> each.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a4e4bd5f845e411f31d8e7dcc2129ff7938a5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> in baggage fees were collected in total, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/0471a6ecf051dff403295052f09051d100d81e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20x + (245 - x) \\times 27 = 5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef7dc80ebbb8d2e9595c9588c82a671479cbd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20x + 245 \\times 27 - 27x = 5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c97cc0c0e56a698ca435713c10b7abae801aff9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-7x + 6615 = 5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12dfc365b9b8ef0cdf2d3411dfeb6859c947fbe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-7x = 5173 - 6615 = -1442$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3ed4458c740a8b123d8b30c315fe156956da294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{-1442}{-7} = 206$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"142\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>The number of people that checked two bags is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4a7a2f6d951f0b42f9bbe17f236da6fe73590f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$245 - x = 245 - 206 = \\boxed{39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"216\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can determine that the number of passengers on the plane would have been <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/4129eebb0569e831f5875a3c47a0b96cf6903768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$245$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. However, we can instead let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of passengers that checked two bags. This makes the number of passengers that checked one bag <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a606048188330b78bf95cbe08c39351e7cee07a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$245 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using similar logic as <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2014 CEMC Galois Problems/Problem 2a\">part a</a>, the passengers that checked one bag would have paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555360df10d7f3448442d43c277f763b0d1236bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> each, while the passengers that checked two bags would have paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30a9e03ced4d2b7794f7535308a84a17d0a06c39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> each.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a4e4bd5f845e411f31d8e7dcc2129ff7938a5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> in baggage fees were collected in total, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6fc76baa41855767dace7ad74717cdeac1cbd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27x + (245 - x) \\times 20 = 5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfe59f61e616335dbf3ead137955f794556b2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27x + 245 \\times 20 - 20x = 5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9addce889cf7f511222623a0262e930979d001ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x + 4900 = 5173$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/1513ba2b768941b44ae63f3e513cb3e83d956a98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7x = 273$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9004a6384713d35d81e040b787587232010831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{273}{7} = \\boxed{39}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 107/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 363/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4252/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.469      1 2014_CEMC_Galois_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    6.469      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35632:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234444 and revision id 278077. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}